hello, i want to make a fun pie chart on jupyter noebook, can you give me an easy example and tell me what each step means

Here is a quick, easy example using Matplotlib, the most common library for making charts in Python.

Step-by-Step Code
Python
# Step 1: Import the plotting library
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Step 2: Define your data
activities = ['Sleeping', 'Coding', 'Eating', 'Overthinking']
hours = [8, 7, 3, 6]
colors = ['#4F81BD', '#C0504D', '#9BBB59', '#8064A2']
explode = (0, 0, 0, 0.1)  # "Pops out" the 4th slice (Overthinking)

# Step 3: Create the pie chart
plt.figure(figsize=(6, 6))
plt.pie(
    hours, 
    labels=activities, 
    autopct='%1.1f%%', 
    startangle=140, 
    colors=colors, 
    explode=explode,
    shadow=True
)

# Step 4: Add a title and show the chart
plt.title('How My Day Is Spent', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')
plt.show()
What Each Step Means
Importing the Library (import matplotlib.pyplot as plt)
matplotlib.pyplot is Python’s standard visualization module. We give it the alias plt so we don't have to type out matplotlib.pyplot every time.

Setting Up the Data

activities: A list of text labels for each slice of the pie.

hours: The actual numerical values that determine how large each slice will be relative to the total sum.

colors: Hex codes (or simple names like 'red', 'blue') to make the chart look nice.

explode: Tells Matplotlib to pull a slice out from the center. 0.1 offsets the 4th item (Overthinking), giving it a dramatic focus.

Building the Chart (plt.pie(...))

autopct='%1.1f%%': Automatically formats and displays the calculated percentages inside each slice with 1 decimal place (e.g., 33.3%).

startangle=140: Rotates the starting point of the first slice counter-clockwise by 140 degrees so the layout looks balanced.

shadow=True: Adds a drop shadow beneath the pie for a 3D effect.

Displaying (plt.title & plt.show())

plt.title(...): Adds a main header above the chart.

plt.show(): Renders the final figure cleanly inside your Jupyter Notebook cell output.

